uncomfortable reshoots accusations of  dishonesty disagreements about directors  these are just some of the reasons these  actors were miserable while shooting a  thor movie keep watching to learn  everything you need to know about the  who and why the most recent thor movies  are known for being lighter and more fun  than many other mcu films the latest  entry thor love and thunder is no  exception from its guardians of the  galaxy hijinks to the hilarious giant  screaming  goats and giant coats look at those they  are wonderful reviewers have praised  this lighthearted take colliders perry  nemeroff posted about the film loads of  laughs my face legit hurts menace of  christian bale's gore is chilling but  most of all loved that it's a film  brimming with good vibes and heart but  that doesn't mean the thor movies have  always been fun to make for all the  actors involved while these films look  like they must have been a blast to  create the intense level of pressure  involved along with issues behind the  scenes means that it wasn't all fun for  everyone on set take for example  christopher eccleston you may know him  best for playing the ninth doctor with  the catchphrase  he famously did not think his experience  on doctor who was fantastic though he  also didn't like being malikith the  accursed the ruler of the dark elves and  thor the dark world for his thor woes  the actor blames a bit of dishonesty  during negotiations he told metro that  he was led to believe there would only  be a little makeup he said what they  didn't say was that it'd be seven hours  of it which was very dishonest of them  that was a miserable experience and a  dreadful performance metro isn't the  only media outlet he complained to he  explained to the guardian how horrible  his experiences were on both gi joe the  rise of cobra in which he played destro  and thor the dark world saying both  roles were regrettable however eccleston  has also made clear that he has no beef  with the cast and crew of the dark world  singling out director alan taylor and  star chris hemsworth for praise he told  metro i loved working with allen he's a  great director and hemsworth was  fantastic a generous actor who really  had his feet on the ground considering  he's appeared in multiple mcu films you  might think idris elba who plays the  asgardian heimdall the former guardian  of the bifrost bridge had a great time  yet like eccleston he said some harsh  things about thor the dark world  specifically elba told the telegraph in  2014 that right after he finished  playing activist nelson mandela in  mandela long walk to freedom he was  contractually obligated to return to the  2013 thor sequel for reshoots this  included an uncomfortable scene in which  he was falling from a spaceship elba  explained i was like this is torture man  i don't want to do this 24 hours ago i  was mandela then there i was in this  stupid harness with this wig and the  sword and these contact lenses it ripped  my heart out even so elba has also  praised taylor and his vision for the  dark world in a flicks and the city  interview and given his continued  presence in the mcu after that it seems  like his issues with the thor reshoots  might have been more situational rather  than a deeper resentment in fact it's  clear the actor wants more work in the  marvel universe not less in 2017 he told  entertainment weekly i like what i have  but i also wish that i had a bigger  character in the marvel universe  there is always hope  one more actor who wasn't thrilled with  the dark world was natalie portman who  became disenchanted with the thor  franchise and reportedly declined to  show up for reshoots for the sequel she  didn't appear in any more marvel films  setting aside a cameo that reused dark  world footage in avengers end game until  love and thunder she also made her beef  public in 2011 the hollywood reporter  reported that portman was deeply unhappy  that her choice for the sequel's  director patty jenkins who would go on  to direct wonder woman was ousted by  marvel following creative differences  the publication said that portman had  already been on the fence about  returning to the franchise because she  wanted to spend time with her family  while vulture noted that she gained a  renewed excitement about the role when  jenkins was hired once jenkins was gone  this presumably changed us reports that  when she said filming conflicts  prevented her from returning for  reshoots hemsworth's real-life wife elsa  pataki filled in for her in an interview  with the wall street journal in 2016  portman said i don't know if one day  they'll ask for an avenger 7 or whatever  i have no idea but as far as i know i'm  done it was a great thing to be a part  of but she obviously had enough fond  memories to finally come back to the  role in love and thunder once jane was  finally given a bigger role according to  cnn it reportedly only took one meeting  for taika ytt to convince her to sign up  again  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the mcu are coming soon subscribe to our  youtube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

